    <string name="help_custom_source_parse_title">Parse Mode Reference</string>
    <string name="help_custom_source_parse_b1">pansou_template: compatible with PanSou API response format. This format places the resource list under the data field, with each resource containing title, url, type, etc.</string>
    <string name="help_custom_source_parse_b2">zreso_template: compatible with ZReso API response format. This format places the resource list under the data.list field, with possibly different field names.</string>
    <string name="help_custom_source_parse_b3">custom: custom mode, requires JSONPath expressions (e.g. $.data.results) to parse JSON response yourself.</string>
    <string name="help_custom_source_parse_pansou_example">pansou_template format example:\n{\n  "data": [\n    {\n      "title": "Movie Name",\n      "url": "https://pan.quark.cn/xxx",\n      "type": "quark",\n      "datetime": "2024-01-01"\n    }\n  ]\n}</string>
    <string name="help_custom_source_parse_zreso_example">zreso_template format example:\n{\n  "data": {\n    "list": [\n      {\n        "name": "Movie Name",\n        "url": "https://pan.baidu.cn/xxx",\n        "cloud_type": "baidu"\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}</string>
    <string name="help_custom_source_example_title">Custom Mode Example</string>
    <string name="help_custom_source_example">If API returns JSON:\n{"data": {"results": [{"title": "Movie Name", "url": "https://...", "type": "quark"}]}}\n\nConfig:\n  parseMode = custom\n  listPath = $.data.results\n  namePath = $.title\n  urlPath = $.url\n  diskTypePath = $.type</string>
