    <string name="statistics_info">Statistics Guide</string>
    <string name="statistics_info_overview">Q: What do the numbers above mean?\nA: They show your total watched count (movies + shows), this month\'s watched count, and this year\'s watched count, based on your Trakt history.</string>
    <string name="statistics_info_heatmap">Q: What is the watching heatmap?\nA: Similar to GitHub\'s contribution graph, each square represents one day. The darker the color, the more you watched that day. It covers the past year.</string>
    <string name="statistics_info_genre_distribution">Q: What is the genre distribution pie chart?\nA: It shows the proportion of each genre in your watched history. Tap a slice to see the exact count and percentage.</string>
    <string name="statistics_info_genre_ranking">Q: What is the top genres ranking?\nA: Your most-watched genres ranked by count. The top three are marked with gold, silver, and bronze medals.</string>
    <string name="statistics_info_watch_time">Q: How is watch time calculated?\nA: It sums up the runtime of every movie and episode you watched, displayed in hours.</string>
    <string name="statistics_info_ratings">Q: What are rating statistics?\nA: Shows your total number of ratings, average rating, and rating distribution on Trakt. Only rated titles are counted.</string>

